{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Echo Show 8 felt useful because a display could help me view compatible cameras and control devices alongside my existing Fire TV setup.",
    "The smart plug offered a small, practical addition: I could try voice control for a lamp without buying another speaker. The Blink bundle also connected to my security interests, especially its doorbell, if it fits my existing setup and coverage needs."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Standalone Echo speakers did not address a clear need. Sharing Alexa with my existing devices is not enough to make me want a separate speaker.",
    "Another 4K Fire TV Stick matched my interests but duplicated equipment I already have, while the HD stick offered less capability. The tablet and Echo Auto did not connect to a current home viewing or security need."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My Amazon device purchases seemed to be treated as interest in almost anything with Alexa, even when its purpose was unrelated to what I use at home.",
    "My streaming purchases seemed to suggest I wanted more streaming devices, without enough attention to whether they would add anything useful."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "What I already own matters: another streaming device needs a clear purpose or improvement to justify adding it.",
    "I am more interested in practical additions to my home entertainment and security setup than expanding into every connected device. Camera compatibility, uncovered areas, and a specific use matter before I would buy a bundle."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "You recognized my interest in connected home entertainment and security, but stretched it into broad Alexa interest and gave too little weight to what I already own."
}"}
